{"author": "pgaudet", "body": "Dear all, \n\nThe proposal has been made to obsolete \nGO:0046501 protoporphyrinogen IX metabolic process\nGO:0006782 protoporphyrinogen IX biosynthetic process\nGO:0019353 protoporphyrinogen IX biosynthetic process from glutamate\nGO:0019352 protoporphyrinogen IX biosynthetic process from glycine\n\nsee https://github.com/geneontology/go-ontology/issues/31788\n\nThe reason for obsoletion is that protoporphyrinogen IX is an intermediate in heme/chlorophyll/uroporphyrinogen synthesis, and genes are better annotated to the BPs for those pathways. There are 29 EXP annotations to these terms (some have already been fixed)\n\nAnnotations are here: \nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1DS39vN-uxcKi1oDABhB2HCTEm5PZfCwka2nEL-5Ezkk/edit?gid=0#gid=0\n\n**EXP annotations**\nBHF-UCL\t1 - done\nEcoCyc\t6\nEcoliWiki\t1\nMGI\t8\nRGD\t2\nUniProt (Noctua)\t6\n\n**Mappings:** \nInterPro\t1\nHAMAP\t7\nUniRule\t11\n", "created_at": "2026-04-02T15:02:41Z", "key": "issue", "labels": [], "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "title": "Review annotations to GO:0046501: protoporphyrinogen IX metabolic process & children", "type": "issue", "updated_at": "2026-04-22T13:24:43Z"}
